From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ios-blink-sideload <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:29:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS sideload: make translation available

Several things kept Chrome's translate feature off in this build.

TranslateManager refuses to offer translation when the build has no
Google API key. The key is not needed: the translate element that
Chrome injects into the page (translate.googleapis.com/translate_a/
element.js and the main script it loads) sends its translateHtml
requests with a key hard-coded in that script, not the one Chrome
passes in. Default the existing ignore-missing-key switch to on.

With Blink, ios/web injects Chrome's page scripts (JavaScriptFeatures)
only behind kContentEnableInjectedFeatureScripts, which is off by
default, so there is no page language detection and no translate
script. Turning it on would inject all 30-odd features; under
ios/web/content their scripts all run in the page's own world, and
each costs jitless V8 time on every page load. Instead, with the flag
off, inject just language detection and translate plus what their
scripts build on (the gCrWeb base and the window.webkit.messageHandlers
shim), let ContentWebFrame call into those two, and always set
__gCrWeb.frameId, which their messages use to name the sending frame.

The Blink side of the JavaScript bridge was also unfinished upstream:
JavaScriptFeature::CallJavaScriptFunction() and ExecuteJavaScript()
just returned false with Blink (TODO crbug.com/40254930), and
ContentWebFrame still called page functions as
__gCrWeb.<api>.<function>(), which gCrWeb no longer provides (it keeps
registered APIs in a private registry). Forward the feature calls to
the frame, and call page functions through
__gCrWeb.callFunctionInGcrWeb() as WebKit's WebFrameImpl does.

Status: verified at Chromium 4558926c in the iOS 27 simulator (with
the system proxy patch, so the simulator reaches Google): on a German
page the "Translate this page?" prompt appears, and translating from
the prompt or the menu turns the text into Chinese.

